  "_commit": {
    "id": "b2a9c29347875328747406aca3cf208872431a75",
    "author": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "committer": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "message": "fix: correct spatialJoin's sparse path for two out-of-core DuckDBDataFrames (0.99.27)\n\nspatialJoin(DuckDBDataFrame, DuckDBDataFrame) with its default\nsparse = TRUE called DuckDBSpatial::st_intersects_table(x, y), which only\never accepted y as a single scalar geometry (sfc/sfg/WKT) -- it has no\ncase for another lazy table. It always errored with \"unsupported\ngeometry type: DuckDBDataFrame\" when both sides were out-of-core,\ndefeating the whole point of the sparse, stay-lazy path (the\nsparse = FALSE branch, a full attribute join via sf::st_join(), already\nworked fine). It also silently ignored the join= predicate argument on\nthis branch regardless.\n\nFixed by switching to DuckDBSpatial::st_join_table() (new in DuckDBSpatial\n0.99.8), a real two-table SQL join producing a sparse (id_x, id_y) pair\ntable instead of embedding y as a literal, which also correctly threads\njoin= through this time.\n",
    "time": 1792513896
  },
